        "original_id": "aa40b025-cfaa-5ec9-8e8a-8704f0f965b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Elvey, Arthur Lubin\n- Roles: film director, producer\n- Works: Abbott & Costello films, Phantom of the Opera, Francis the Talking Mule, Mister Ed\n- Topics: British film history, American film and television\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Elvey was born on 11 November 1887 and died on 28 August 1967.\n- Arthur Lubin was born on July 25, 1898 and died on May 12, 1995.\n- Maurice Elvey was the most prolific film director in British history.\n- Arthur Lubin was an American film director and producer.\n- Arthur Lubin directed several Abbott & Costello films.\n- Arthur Lubin directed Phantom of the Opera in 1943.\n- Arthur Lubin directed the Francis the Talking Mule series.\n- Arthur Lubin created the talking-horse TV series Mister Ed.",
